ef 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186112039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186112039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186112039 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186112039 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186112039 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186528894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186112039 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8abb5688-150a-50b2-9719-9f49715e34e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115100 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5121" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115100 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\dfrac {x^2 - 9} {(x + 3)(x+2)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115100 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1eaa26ba-0958-58db-9f30-35a33f98f2d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115100 #edb/ref 1074 "The numerator is a difference of squares. If we factor it and then cancel out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {x^2 - 9} {(x + 3)(x+2)}  & = \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {(x + 3)(x - 3)} {(x + 3)(x+2)}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {\\cancel{(x + 3)}(x - 3)} {\\cancel{(x + 3)}(x+2)}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {x - 3} {x+2} &. \\\t\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115101 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5122" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115101 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\dfrac {x^2 + x - 6} {x-2}$ reduced to lowest terms?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115101 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fb69899e-6aee-5128-973e-e19792a1cbdb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115101 #edb/ref 1074 "The numerator can be factored as $x^2+x-6= (x+3)(x-2).$ Cancelling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-6}{x-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)(x-2)}{x-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{(x-2)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x+3}{1} & = \\\\ x+3 & .\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115102 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5123" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115102 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2a^2+4ab+2b^2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115102 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd181873-1190-5ffa-b2aa-c7eb68c1255c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115102 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we take out a factor of $2$ from the denominator, and then use the polynomial factorization $a^2+2ab+b^2 = (a+b)^2.$ Cancelling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2a^2+4ab+2b^2}\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2\\left(a^2+2ab+b^2\\right)} \\\n                &=\\dfrac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot(a+b)} {2(a+b)(a+b)} \\\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot\\cancel{(a+b)}} {\\cancel{2}\\cancel{(a+b)}(a+b)}\\\n\t\t&=\\dfrac {2} {a+b}.\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115104 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5313" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115104 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x^2-5x+6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115104 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e777ba3-6a10-5c47-b069-ee33a6892a98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115104 #edb/ref 1074 "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n![](images/39/39c702fb9697e87abfb8bbfb1a4bfbec813a0f4ffbe47d3ea90b56adfdd371a0.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115271 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115271 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115271 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115271 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115271 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115271 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115271 #edb/ref 1039 "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Difference of Squares in the Numerator" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115271 #edb