92186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529098 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+4}{4x-4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529098 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1950cd5e-6ddb-5e2d-959e-224740d86f48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529098 #edb/ref 1074 "The numerator can be factored as\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-8x+4=4({x}^{2}-2x+1)=4(x-1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+4}{4x-4} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)^{2}}{4(x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)(x-1)}{4(x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4(x-1)}(x-1)}{\\cancel{4(x-1)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{1} & = \\\\ x-1. & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529110 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529110 #edb/ref 1069 "q-29819" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529110 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529110 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{a+b}{7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529110 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "33d475f4-4da4-572d-a596-bce698fbb9fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529110 #edb/ref 1074 "The denominator can be factored as the difference of squares: \n\n$$\n7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}=7({a}^{2}-{b}^{2})=7(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a+b}{7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}} & =\\frac{a+b}{7(a+b)(a-b)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(a+b)}}{7\\cancel{(a+b)}(a-b)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7(a-b)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529141 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186529025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529141 #edb/ref 1069 "q-79524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529141 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529141 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\frac{{a}^{2}-4a+4}{{a}^{2}-4}$ reduced to lowest terms?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529141 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77fb920e-43ca-5282-8a0a-596d7af0b021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529141 #edb/ref 1074 "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}^{2}-4a+4}{{a}^{2}-4} & =\\frac{(a-2)^{2}}{(a-2)(a+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(a-2)\\cancel{(a-2)}}{\\cancel{(a-2)}(a+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{a-2}{a+2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529154 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186529006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529154 #edb/ref 1069 "q-29824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529154 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529154 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\frac{{z}^{2}-6z+9}{3-z}$ reduced to lowest terms?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529154 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "97b7ba7e-3c98-5de8-abc1-d6b6edb5c45e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529154 #edb/ref 1074 "The numerator can be factored as\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}-6z+9=(z-3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}-6z+9}{3-z} & = \\\\ -\\frac{{z}^{2}-6z+9}{z-3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{z-3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{\\cancel{(z-3)}(z-3)}{\\cancel{z-3}} & = \\\\ -\\frac{z-3}{1} & = \\\\ 3-z. & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529169 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529169 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113063" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529169 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529169 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\frac{3t-15}{3{t}^{2}-30t+75}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529169 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c85a34c5-6e9b-5e37-9be6-8bd5b320956b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529169 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we take out a factor of $3$ from the numerator and from the denominator, and then use the polynomial factorization ${t}^{2}-10t+25=(t-5)^{2}.$ Canceling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3t-15}{3{t}^{2}-30t+75} & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3({t}^{2}-10t+25)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3(t-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3(t-5)(t-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}\\cancel{(t-5)}}{\\cancel{3}\\cancel{(t-5)}(t-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
